a new book on hbo has given an insight  into the fact that george r.r martin was  not happy with the direction that game  of thrones took towards the end of its  run  in particular the final three seasons  took scrutiny from the acclaimed author  james andrew miller's new book tinderbox  hbo's ruthless pursuit of new frontiers  explores the fact that martin fills his  templates for seasons beyond the  original books plot were largely ignored  the show only had material up to season  six  at this point show runners david benioff  and d.b vice needed to continue writing  for the show with essentially a blank  slate and ideas from martin  it appears as though according to george  r martin's representative paul hass he  felt the show's writers didn't follow  his intentions  hass details in the book that george  loves dan and dave but after season five  he did start to worry about the path  they were going down because george  knows where the story goes  he started saying  you're not following my template the  first five seasons stuck to george's  road map then they went off george's  road map  fans seem to echo martin's concerns as  it's widely known that the last three  seasons came under criticism in  comparison to what came before  the rushed ending of season 7  particularly came under the spotlight  for scrutiny  the book goes on to give more  information about martin's suggestion  that there should have been 10 seasons  of the hbo show to give the writers more  freedom to tie up loose ends  paul hass gives an insight into this as  well as he states  george would fly to new york to have  lunch with former hbo ceo richard  pleppler to beg him to do 10 seasons of  10 episodes because there was enough  material for it and to tell him it would  be a more satisfying and more  entertaining experience  it's clear that martin wanted the show  to run much longer than the 73 episodes  that it did  and has even mentioned in an interview  to variety that he had ideas that could  take the epic to 13 seasons  in the end hass puts the fact that it  only ran to eight down to the fact that  show runners vice and benioff were tired  and wanted to move on with other  projects  it seems as though the network agreed  with martin that they wanted more shows  but the writers wanted to wrap it up  despite the fact that the original game  of thrones run is complete this hasn't  stopped several other related tv  projects from approaching our screens  steve conrad has recently been announced  as executive producer on the adaptation  of martin's duncan egg series a prequel  to game of thrones  amongst other shows conrad is  responsible for the amazon series  patriot on top of current amc stop  motion animation series ultra city  smiths  it seems hbo are busy with game of  thrones prequels at the moment as these  also include 10 000 ships sea snake as  well as three untitled animated series  for hbo max  let me know your thoughts on this latest  news in the comments section down below  and stay tuned for more game of thrones  content
 

